# A ring of modules, panel 252's R1 (2026-11-19): a face, `geom`, uses its
# private module `geom/internal/calc`, and the private module names the
# face's own record, `geom.Point`, through `use geom`. Until that sitting the
# second `use` was `error[module_cycle]`, and Rebel's packages wrote a mirror
# of their faces' types instead. `calc` adds one to the sum of the squares.
use geom

function main()
    p = geom.origin()
    print(geom.norm(p))
